WEBVTT

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:11.687
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.487
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:21.177
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.277 --> 00:00:28.907
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:33.247
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.127
But, with you...

00:00:35.127 --> 00:00:37.207
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:42.797
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:47.517
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:51.897
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:53.477
Just to survive!

00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:55.437
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.437 --> 00:00:57.277
Take this moment...

00:00:57.277 --> 00:01:00.897
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:03.107
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.107 --> 00:01:04.947
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.947 --> 00:01:08.657
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.657 --> 00:01:10.787
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:12.497
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.497 --> 00:01:16.167
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.337
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:20.167
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:24.087
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:32.976 --> 00:01:37.214
I’m challenging the allegedly
difficult DDS admissions test!

00:01:37.781 --> 00:01:40.784
During the first exam, using the photograph
of the crime scene we saw on the screen…

00:01:40.784 --> 00:01:42.853
…I managed to work out the culprit’s identity.

00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:46.723
My friends Megu, Kinta, Kazuma and I tailed him.

00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:52.796
But, having done that, can we find the
location of the second exam in time?

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.831
If we don’t we won’t qualify!

00:01:55.932 --> 00:01:56.633
And now…

00:02:08.011 --> 00:02:08.879
You guys alright?

00:02:09.012 --> 00:02:09.513
Yeah.

00:02:10.147 --> 00:02:11.615
How’s this for an elementary school kid?

00:02:11.748 --> 00:02:12.883
Sticking with us?

00:02:13.116 --> 00:02:14.651
Yeah, somehow…

00:02:21.758 --> 00:02:23.527
Ow... Ow... Ow...

00:02:25.362 --> 00:02:26.496
Saburoumaru-san!

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.766
Well if it isn’t the Tokyo University
student with the 180 IQ!

00:02:31.268 --> 00:02:32.736
Ah, so you guys are here too?

00:02:33.036 --> 00:02:36.439
So we aren’t the only ones who’ve
made it this far then?

00:02:36.606 --> 00:02:37.874
Just lick Tokyo University student!

00:02:38.275 --> 00:02:42.879
That means that we’re at the same level
as a Tokyo University student, right?

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.414
That's so great!

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:47.184
I think that theory is slightly mistaken.

00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:50.987
Are you okay? Let me help you up.

00:02:55.859 --> 00:02:58.795
It’s not my nature to accept sympathy from others.

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:01.865
As repayment, I'll be your guide.

00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:06.136
Megu, are you really friends with him?

00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:08.271
Huh?

00:03:09.573 --> 00:03:11.841
We’ve lost sight of the culprit…

00:03:13.243 --> 00:03:13.810
Oh crap!

00:03:14.177 --> 00:03:15.178
We’ve gotta hurry!

00:03:15.478 --> 00:03:16.680
Alright, let’s get moving!

00:03:21.084 --> 00:03:21.918
H-Hey!

00:03:29.659 --> 00:03:31.261
What’s up with this cliff?

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:34.764
That guy!

00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:39.035
How did he get across?

00:03:40.937 --> 00:03:43.006
It doesn’t look like there’s a path that crosses it.

00:03:43.607 --> 00:03:46.543
But there’s got to be some way to get across.

00:03:47.277 --> 00:03:49.813
I've got it! I've thought of a good idea!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.081
What is it?

00:03:51.448 --> 00:03:56.319
As a 10-dan in kendo, judo and karate, I will…

00:03:56.853 --> 00:04:00.857
…punch Kyuu, Mega and Kazuma across…

00:04:02.225 --> 00:04:03.326
…to the other side!

00:04:03.526 --> 00:04:06.463
After that, I'll miraculously jump
across with a BIG jump!

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:09.899
How’s that? Good idea, right?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.234
Absolutely not.

00:04:12.235 --> 00:04:12.869
Why not?

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.204
I'll take a pass too.

00:04:14.437 --> 00:04:16.139
Are you thinking about this seriously?

00:04:16.273 --> 00:04:20.110
What’s wrong? I've got the skill of a 10-dan
martial artist. Don’t you believe in me?

00:04:23.813 --> 00:04:27.817
Hey, Kinta, let’s see if we can get across
the ravine using those logs.

00:04:28.485 --> 00:04:29.719
Maybe we could fashion & bridge?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.655
Alright, let’s try it.

00:04:38.862 --> 00:04:41.231
Ah? Ow… Ow… Ow…

00:04:41.231 --> 00:04:45.201
I hurt my hip when I fell off the trail earlier!

00:04:45.802 --> 00:04:46.870
Get well soon…

00:04:48.405 --> 00:04:50.473
Here we go…

00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:54.377
This won’t work. It’s not reaching.

00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:56.646
Just a little further…

00:04:58.281 --> 00:05:01.084
But all of these logs seem to be the same length.

00:05:01.951 --> 00:05:04.788
Ah! That’s it! I know what to do!

00:05:08.391 --> 00:05:11.328
This puzzle can be solved using simple mathematics.

00:05:12.996 --> 00:05:13.730
Is this okay?

00:05:14.264 --> 00:05:16.299
'L’ is the length of the ravine.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.702
’M’ is the length of the logs.

00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:21.071
I've created this diagram.

00:05:21.771 --> 00:05:27.577
And so, if we put these here and the other logs
here, we can build a bridge that will reach.

00:05:28.311 --> 00:05:29.245
Amazing!

00:05:29.512 --> 00:05:31.614
Worthy of a genius programmer!

00:05:31.848 --> 00:05:33.216
It was really nothing…

00:05:33.216 --> 00:05:35.251
Alright! Let’s do it!

00:05:37.721 --> 00:05:38.455
It’s done!

00:05:39.122 --> 00:05:39.856
Alright!

00:05:40.957 --> 00:05:44.894
Well then, I'll go and confirm
the safety of this bridge.

00:05:46.129 --> 00:05:46.796
Wait a sec!

00:05:52.769 --> 00:05:55.038
Everyone, I'm going on ahead…

00:05:56.172 --> 00:05:57.273
What’s up with him?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.441
Ah, it’s alright.

00:05:59.109 --> 00:06:01.811
Well, he just confirmed the stability of the bridge…

00:06:02.345 --> 00:06:04.147
Now, let’s all cross it too!

00:06:06.116 --> 00:06:07.951
Now that I think about it, this really is high…

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:10.653
Don’t look down! Don’t look down!

00:06:11.755 --> 00:06:14.190
It’s dangerous to look down…

00:06:17.193 --> 00:06:17.861
Alright!

00:06:18.661 --> 00:06:20.296
Alright!!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.733
We all showed pretty good teamwork, didn’t we?

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.034
Seems so.

00:06:25.301 --> 00:06:30.106
Maybe this test is supposed to determine
our ability to work together!

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.242
Now, let’s hurry on!

00:06:34.544 --> 00:06:37.547
Alright! If I can keep it like
this, I'll have a good lead!

00:06:38.848 --> 00:06:39.249
Huh?

00:06:41.084 --> 00:06:42.352
I've caught up!

00:06:45.388 --> 00:06:45.822
Hmm?

00:06:46.723 --> 00:06:49.292
The weight limit is 90 kilograms…

00:06:51.094 --> 00:06:52.929
I might be able to use this…

00:06:54.197 --> 00:07:00.437
Now I, Saburoumaru Yutaka-sama, with
my 180 IQ, will be the only one to pass!

00:07:08.278 --> 00:07:11.047
Thank goodness. This time there’s
already a bridge here.

00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:14.651
But it looks kind of dangerous somehow…

00:07:15.185 --> 00:07:19.022
Ah, it looks like it’ll be fine. Take a look at this.

00:07:19.622 --> 00:07:24.594
The weight limit is 290 kilograms. If it’s
just the four of us it should be fine.

00:07:25.395 --> 00:07:26.596
Then let’s hurry and catch up!

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:28.331
Alright, let’s go!

00:07:28.865 --> 00:07:31.901
Though, I still think it would be
better if we go one at a time…

00:07:32.168 --> 00:07:34.137
If we do that we’ll fall behind.

00:07:34.671 --> 00:07:35.305
It’ll be ﬁne.

00:07:42.078 --> 00:07:44.180
Hey, what’s up with these noises?

00:07:51.521 --> 00:07:52.055
Run for it!

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:04.834
Gotcha!

00:08:06.002 --> 00:08:07.303
Up you go!

00:08:07.303 --> 00:08:08.872
I knew this was going to be bad!

00:08:14.677 --> 00:08:16.045
Kyuu! Megu!

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:18.114
I'm coming for you now!

00:08:19.916 --> 00:08:21.818
We’re fine! Go on ahead of us!

00:08:22.552 --> 00:08:24.220
I'm confident in my swimming ability!

00:08:28.691 --> 00:08:30.593
Kyuu-san. Megu-san.

00:08:31.995 --> 00:08:34.297
I can’t believe this. Seriously? You can’t swim?

00:08:34.664 --> 00:08:37.433
I take ultimate pride in not being
able to swim a stroke!

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.369
What’s boasting like that going to do for you?

00:08:39.369 --> 00:08:41.137
Whatever! Help me!

00:08:42.672 --> 00:08:43.239
Hey!

00:08:44.173 --> 00:08:46.476
Geez,! guess I have no choice…

00:08:49.712 --> 00:08:52.749
You’re really a life-saver, Megu.

00:08:53.182 --> 00:08:56.452
It usually goes the other way.
How shameful of you.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:02.625
Are you sure those two will be okay?

00:09:03.159 --> 00:09:06.229
You shouldn’t give up on them so easily.

00:09:07.063 --> 00:09:11.501
But there isn’t much time left
to get to the second exam.

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:12.535
Oh yeah.

00:09:13.236 --> 00:09:15.738
We’d better start looking for it soon ourselves.

00:09:16.506 --> 00:09:17.073
Let’s hurry!

00:09:17.273 --> 00:09:18.841
Hey, please wait for me!

00:09:24.814 --> 00:09:25.815
Up I go.

00:09:27.216 --> 00:09:28.685
Thanks a lot, Megu.

00:09:28.985 --> 00:09:30.920
But, where are we, I wonder.

00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:35.625
We should be fine. I'm pretty sure we’re
not far from Kinta and Kazuma.

00:09:35.858 --> 00:09:36.859
Let’s hurry.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:37.694
Yeah.

00:09:41.397 --> 00:09:44.467
We’ve got about 30 minutes left
to get to the second exam.

00:09:46.002 --> 00:09:47.203
What should we do?

00:09:48.705 --> 00:09:50.006
Hey, look!

00:09:50.073 --> 00:09:50.940
What is it?

00:09:50.974 --> 00:09:52.909
Look! Over there!

00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:54.010
Huh?

00:09:54.477 --> 00:09:55.979
Ah! That’s Kinta-san’s!

00:09:56.379 --> 00:09:59.148
Kinta left markers telling us which way to go.

00:09:59.148 --> 00:10:02.552
Thank goodness! I thought we were done for!

00:10:02.986 --> 00:10:04.320
These will lead us to the second exam.

00:10:04.754 --> 00:10:05.088
Yeah!

00:10:05.421 --> 00:10:06.522
Hey!

00:10:08.791 --> 00:10:10.093
What was that just now?

00:10:12.528 --> 00:10:14.631
Hey! Help me please!

00:10:15.131 --> 00:10:15.598
This way!

00:10:20.503 --> 00:10:23.506
Hey, you guys! Could you help me out?

00:10:24.107 --> 00:10:25.341
What happened?

00:10:26.075 --> 00:10:28.678
I lost my footing for a second and fell…

00:10:29.145 --> 00:10:32.382
I think I may have broken my leg and I can’t move.

00:10:32.548 --> 00:10:34.684
He’s in trouble. We’ve got to help!

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:35.218
Yeah.

00:10:35.485 --> 00:10:37.353
Hold on, mister!

00:10:43.926 --> 00:10:44.761
What’s the matter?

00:10:45.628 --> 00:10:47.363
Let’s keep going, Megu.

00:10:48.598 --> 00:10:51.801
If we help him, we won’t make
it in time for the second exam.

00:10:51.934 --> 00:10:56.172
What are you saying? Are you saying we should
abandon someone who’s been injured?

00:10:57.006 --> 00:10:57.573
Yes.

00:10:58.007 --> 00:10:59.375
That’s terrible!

00:10:59.475 --> 00:11:03.680
I must have misjudged you! You think can
pass the exam if you leave him like this?

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.983
That’s not it! I think we’re supposed
to leave him there.

00:11:07.116 --> 00:11:09.085
Supposed to leave him here?

00:11:09.719 --> 00:11:11.688
Please trust me.

00:11:14.824 --> 00:11:15.525
Trust me.

00:11:16.893 --> 00:11:20.063
Okay, but tell me the reason.

00:11:20.296 --> 00:11:22.432
Okay. There are two hints.

00:11:23.032 --> 00:11:27.270
Ah, now’s not the time to explain
them. ln any case, let’s go!

00:11:27.704 --> 00:11:28.471
Y-yeah!

00:11:29.706 --> 00:11:30.840
Hey, you guys!

00:11:31.374 --> 00:11:34.277
Where are you going? You’re not going to help me?

00:11:42.318 --> 00:11:42.952
It’s me.

00:11:44.687 --> 00:11:47.156
Let’s leave a marker for them around here too!

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:48.124
Okay!

00:11:52.528 --> 00:11:54.363
Alright! Okay, let’s go!

00:11:55.765 --> 00:12:00.737
At present there are three people who have made
it to the final point for the second test.

00:12:01.504 --> 00:12:03.406
Another two just passed by.

00:12:03.973 --> 00:12:05.708
They should be arriving shortly.

00:12:06.542 --> 00:12:07.210
Roger.

00:12:07.276 --> 00:12:09.412
Someone will pick you up in about ten minutes.

00:12:09.679 --> 00:12:10.346
I understand.

00:12:15.618 --> 00:12:17.887
Wait a sec! So that’s what was going on.

00:12:18.488 --> 00:12:19.088
Yep.

00:12:19.756 --> 00:12:22.492
Even though it seemed we should
help him, it was a trick.

00:12:23.192 --> 00:12:24.527
That was most likely part of the exam.

00:12:25.161 --> 00:12:28.931
That’s just like you, Kyuu! He almost tricked me.

00:12:30.633 --> 00:12:31.300
What’s the matter?

00:12:33.169 --> 00:12:35.037
Megu, go on ahead of me.

00:12:35.705 --> 00:12:36.739
Where are you going?

00:12:36.939 --> 00:12:40.176
Ah, well… I swallowed lots of water while
we were swimming, so I have to go pee.

00:12:40.309 --> 00:12:41.310
Go on ahead!

00:12:42.545 --> 00:12:44.514
Geez! Be quick about it.

00:12:52.054 --> 00:12:52.922
That sound…

00:12:58.127 --> 00:12:59.662
Oh no! That sound!

00:13:05.802 --> 00:13:07.003
Will I make it in time?

00:13:20.216 --> 00:13:22.585
The water will probably came up this far.

00:13:22.618 --> 00:13:24.787
I have to get to higher ground somehow

00:13:34.397 --> 00:13:35.097
It’s you!

00:13:38.534 --> 00:13:40.403
Mister, hurry on up here!

00:13:56.818 --> 00:13:59.121
Those two haven’t come yet.

00:13:59.521 --> 00:14:03.458
What could they be doing? The
exam is about to begin…

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:04.927
Ah?

00:14:05.961 --> 00:14:06.995
Oh, Megu!

00:14:07.596 --> 00:14:09.831
Kinta-san! Kazuma-kun!

00:14:10.365 --> 00:14:11.400
You’re late!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:12.801
Sorry, sorry!

00:14:14.503 --> 00:14:15.337
You’re alone?

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.372
What happened to Kyuu? Where’s Kyuu?

00:14:17.873 --> 00:14:19.308
He’s not here yet?

00:14:19.374 --> 00:14:22.978
He went to take a leak in the
forest and never came back.

00:14:23.378 --> 00:14:25.714
I thought he came here ahead of me.

00:14:25.981 --> 00:14:27.749
Did he have an upset stomach?

00:14:28.183 --> 00:14:29.518
Oh dang, it’s time.

00:14:29.985 --> 00:14:31.053
Let’s head on inside.

00:14:31.386 --> 00:14:32.688
Ah, yeah…

00:14:38.827 --> 00:14:41.463
That was a close one. Thank you.

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:45.133
No problem. More importantly
mister, are you okay?

00:14:45.367 --> 00:14:45.934
Yes.

00:14:46.668 --> 00:14:48.236
What’s your name?

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.005
I'm Kyuu.

00:14:50.372 --> 00:14:51.306
Kyuu-kun, eh?

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:52.040
Yes.

00:14:52.607 --> 00:14:55.911
Well then Ryan-kun, I have two questions for you.

00:14:56.445 --> 00:14:56.945
Eh?

00:14:57.512 --> 00:15:02.551
The first is, why did you leave me when I claimed
to have a broken bone and asked for help?

00:15:02.851 --> 00:15:07.322
The second is, since you left me the
first time, why did you come back?

00:15:09.524 --> 00:15:11.360
Now, please tell me.

00:15:12.294 --> 00:15:13.128
Okay.

00:15:13.562 --> 00:15:19.701
Well, first off, I knew you weren’t asking me
for help because you had broken a bone.

00:15:20.068 --> 00:15:21.636
Oh, why so?

00:15:21.737 --> 00:15:23.672
That’s because of your shoes.

00:15:25.007 --> 00:15:29.077
Your soles didn’t have any mud on
them at all; they were very clean.

00:15:29.945 --> 00:15:31.179
My shoes, eh?

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:32.914
Yes.

00:15:33.615 --> 00:15:35.784
It would be pretty strange, don’t you think?

00:15:36.251 --> 00:15:38.920
They should have been dirty
if you’d fallen from the trail.

00:15:39.221 --> 00:15:43.892
So I thought it was probably a
trap to eliminate candidates.

00:15:44.292 --> 00:15:45.394
I see.

00:15:46.261 --> 00:15:48.330
And the reason you came back was?

00:15:48.597 --> 00:15:52.200
That was when I heard the flood siren from the dam.

00:15:55.003 --> 00:16:00.175
When I was a kid, I really liked
to play around hills and rivers.

00:16:00.409 --> 00:16:04.413
So I know that when the alarm sounds
the water level will increase rapidly.

00:16:04.413 --> 00:16:06.481
It can be incredibly dangerous.

00:16:06.882 --> 00:16:10.619
So I thought that you might be swept away by it.

00:16:10.819 --> 00:16:15.490
But if what you said is true and that
I really did pretend to be injured…

00:16:15.524 --> 00:16:19.561
…why wouldn’t I have just climbed
up the cliff to get away?

00:16:19.728 --> 00:16:23.432
Well, there’s no mud on your shoes…

00:16:23.832 --> 00:16:25.834
…but they look pretty well worn otherwise.

00:16:26.601 --> 00:16:29.271
However, the soles have no wear
on them at all, do they?

00:16:30.138 --> 00:16:37.045
That means you don’t walk in
them very much, do you?

00:16:37.679 --> 00:16:41.783
For example, maybe you use
a wheelchair or something?

00:16:43.452 --> 00:16:48.457
And, if that were true, it would be impossible
for you to climb the cliff by yourself.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.392
That’s why I hurried back.

00:16:50.926 --> 00:16:54.029
I see. What great deduction skills you have.

00:16:54.029 --> 00:16:57.766
Though, it’s too late to make it to
the second exam because of this.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.168
After making it this far, it’s a pity.

00:17:00.836 --> 00:17:01.636
Don’t be a idiot!

00:17:02.404 --> 00:17:05.841
If you ever give up, a case might
remain unsolved forever!

00:17:06.208 --> 00:17:06.475
Eh?

00:17:07.576 --> 00:17:09.077
It’s too early to give up!

00:17:09.911 --> 00:17:10.545
Mister…

00:17:10.645 --> 00:17:13.448
I'm fine now. Get going!

00:17:15.016 --> 00:17:15.717
Okay!

00:17:20.889 --> 00:17:22.190
Kyuu-kun, eh?

00:17:23.658 --> 00:17:25.327
What an interesting boy.

00:17:37.539 --> 00:17:39.875
What's with all these people here?

00:17:39.941 --> 00:17:44.012
could they have came from some
other place titan the first exam?

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:46.615
I'll…

00:17:47.449 --> 00:17:48.450
...never...

00:17:49.217 --> 00:17:50.252
…give up!

00:17:54.089 --> 00:17:56.892
I feel a bit uncomfortable taking
this without my hat…

00:17:57.125 --> 00:17:59.161
He'll come. He definitely will.

00:17:59.895 --> 00:18:03.064
Kyuu, where could you have gone?

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.869
No! I can’t be detracted now.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:09.671
But...

00:18:21.249 --> 00:18:24.352
Forgive my lateness! Please allow
to me take the test too!

00:18:26.521 --> 00:18:27.289
Kyuu!

00:18:27.856 --> 00:18:30.458
You’ve finally made it.

00:18:30.525 --> 00:18:32.694
You found the coat and hat, right?

00:18:32.861 --> 00:18:36.598
Yeah, thanks to them I made it in time! Thanks a lot!

00:18:36.965 --> 00:18:40.368
Kinta, here! Kazuma-kun, here you go!

00:18:40.735 --> 00:18:41.570
Got it!

00:18:42.771 --> 00:18:46.208
Thank goodness! I wasn’t feeling my best without it.

00:18:46.741 --> 00:18:51.279
You there, there’s only 10 minutes left for
the exam. Do you still want to take it?

00:18:51.479 --> 00:18:56.484
Yes, if a detective gives up, a case might
remain unsolved forever, right?

00:18:57.919 --> 00:19:02.457
What a moron. What does he think
he can do in only 10 minutes?

00:19:03.258 --> 00:19:05.327
Hey, is anyone sitting here?

00:19:05.594 --> 00:19:06.661
Uh? No.

00:19:06.861 --> 00:19:07.429
Good.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.705
Alright, let’s do this!

00:19:28.883 --> 00:19:29.751
Kyuu!

00:19:29.818 --> 00:19:31.519
How did the test go?

00:19:32.153 --> 00:19:35.557
Ah, perfect! I definitely passed!

00:19:35.924 --> 00:19:36.625
Eh?

00:19:36.925 --> 00:19:38.326
You really mean…?

00:19:38.326 --> 00:19:41.129
In just 10 minutes, you solved all the problems?

00:19:41.463 --> 00:19:43.398
Ah, no, I only answered one.

00:19:43.498 --> 00:19:45.400
What? Only one?

00:19:45.667 --> 00:19:47.402
Please don’t joke with us like that.

00:19:47.669 --> 00:19:48.770
I guess you had no choice.

00:19:49.204 --> 00:19:51.206
With only 10 minutes left to work on it.

00:19:51.673 --> 00:19:54.309
It'll be okay. Don’t be depressed about it.

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:56.611
I'm not depressed at all.

00:19:56.945 --> 00:19:57.345
Eh?

00:19:58.113 --> 00:20:01.483
Even though I've done lots of stuff before today…

00:20:01.616 --> 00:20:04.519
…this is the first time I've seriously
tried to become a detective.

00:20:06.087 --> 00:20:12.160
Also, the one question I answered
on the test was really interesting.

00:20:12.527 --> 00:20:14.296
This was more than enough to satisfy me.

00:20:14.496 --> 00:20:16.364
He’s really satisfied by that?

00:20:16.698 --> 00:20:17.799
What a weird guy…

00:20:17.899 --> 00:20:19.434
Just like the guy to the right of me.

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:28.443
Mom’s probably really angry.

00:20:30.979 --> 00:20:32.414
She was really serious.

00:20:37.018 --> 00:20:38.620
I'm really scared!

00:20:41.222 --> 00:20:42.957
Mom, I'm sorry, but I…

00:20:46.728 --> 00:20:50.632
Hurry inside. Dinner’s already on the table.

00:20:52.267 --> 00:20:52.867
Y-Yeah…

00:20:54.502 --> 00:20:56.204
Are you going to take the test again next year?

00:20:56.371 --> 00:20:57.072
Yeah.

00:20:57.772 --> 00:21:00.608
After all, it’s impossible to pass when
I only answered one question.

00:21:00.942 --> 00:21:05.013
Hey Kyuu, why do you want
to be a detective so much?

00:21:05.146 --> 00:21:10.085
That’s because of what happened
earlier, during the kidnapping…

00:21:10.352 --> 00:21:15.724
My dream is to become like the
detective who saved me.

00:21:31.473 --> 00:21:34.743
He was really cool, that guy.

00:21:40.815 --> 00:21:44.552
No matter how many years it takes me, I'll
never give up wanting to be a detective!

00:21:44.819 --> 00:21:47.088
No matter how much you may be opposed to it!

00:21:47.889 --> 00:21:48.656
Time to eat!

00:21:51.626 --> 00:21:52.594
Kyuu…

00:22:00.702 --> 00:22:01.302
Hello.

00:22:02.203 --> 00:22:02.971
That’s right.

00:22:05.573 --> 00:22:06.107
Huh?

00:22:09.878 --> 00:22:11.946
You were right, Katagiri-kun.

00:22:12.514 --> 00:22:16.918
The boy named Kyuu truly is a diamond in the rough.

00:22:17.552 --> 00:22:20.488
You saw this with your own eyes then?

00:22:20.722 --> 00:22:21.022
Yes.

00:22:21.689 --> 00:22:26.828
But he was late for the second exam and
only answered one question, right?

00:22:27.529 --> 00:22:29.864
It must be because he saved your life then?

00:22:30.732 --> 00:22:33.134
I'm not that nice of a person.

00:22:33.768 --> 00:22:35.270
Then, why?

00:22:35.837 --> 00:22:38.940
The question that he answered in only 10 minutes…

00:22:39.307 --> 00:22:44.412
…was from a difficult case that I, Dan Morihiko,
had a hard time with early in my career.

00:22:45.513 --> 00:22:50.685
Of course, eventually, with much effort,
I found the necessary clues.

00:22:52.454 --> 00:22:58.526
But so far, only one other person has
been able to solve that problem.

00:22:59.227 --> 00:23:03.031
That alone makes him qualified to attend.

00:23:10.138 --> 00:23:10.672
No way…

00:23:11.506 --> 00:23:13.875
I've been admitted to the defective academy?

00:23:14.809 --> 00:23:16.544
I don’t believe this!

00:23:17.412 --> 00:23:20.114
Yahoo! Alright! Ha ha!

00:23:20.381 --> 00:23:23.284
Alright! Alright! Alright! Waaaa!

00:23:23.818 --> 00:23:29.958
It’s really true! Woohoo! I really passed! Alright!

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:27.930
I guess he’s still a kid after all.

00:23:36.456 --> 00:23:46.706
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.096 --> 00:24:01.306
Saying I'll always be beside you without saying a single word.

00:24:01.546 --> 00:24:08.636
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:08.636 --> 00:24:14.266
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:14.466 --> 00:24:20.376
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:20.476 --> 00:24:25.926
I will see you off.

00:24:26.176 --> 00:24:35.366
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:36.293 --> 00:24:39.429
Now that we’re all students
of DDS, we have a problem.

00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:44.101
We’ll be up against a bomber who has challenged
the legendary defective, Dan Morihiko.

00:24:44.902 --> 00:24:48.405
We don’t have much time. We have to begin
searching the campus as soon as possible!

00:24:49.239 --> 00:24:51.742
Where did that criminal plant the bomb?

00:24:52.709 --> 00:24:53.810
There’s only one answer!

00:24:59.216 --> 00:25:01.585
Mama, Ryuu’s in the newspaper!

00:25:02.319 --> 00:25:03.987
Please, come here quick!

00:25:05.739 --> 00:25:06.287
Kate!
